    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) standing as our premier offensive anchor. His matchup against Flaherty is ideal; the favorable wind conditions and his leadoff placement amplify his elite sprint speed, which is critical for our pursuit of the stolen base category. **Yordan Alvarez** (78.29) remains a must-start despite a neutral park factor, as his elite 0.476 xwOBA against Junk provides a high floor for power and run production. We are also leaning heavily on **Christian Yelich** (75.76); facing Peralta, he benefits from a slow delivery profile that significantly bolsters his stolen base probability, further reinforcing our strategy of aggressive base-running targeting.\n\nIn the middle infield, **Caleb Durbin** (63.60) is an intriguing play over typical bench depth. His score is bolstered by a favorable matchup against Baz, specifically targeting the latter's slow pace, which yields a tangible boost to **Caleb Durbin**'s projected SB upside. Conversely, **Junior Caminero** (55.20) represents our most volatile start; while he is currently active, he draws Cease, an elite arm with a 2.96 xERA. We are gambling on **Junior Caminero**'s talent and the favorable #3 hole protection, but he remains our most likely candidate for an early pinch-hit substitution if he fails to track the breaking ball.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, with **Chase Meidroth** (32.38) serving as the closest cut. While he provides utility, he fell well below our 40.0 efficiency floor, primarily due to the severe SP skill disadvantage presented by deGrom. We continue to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim**, who remains roster-locked in the minors, alongside **Carson Benge** and **Nelson Velazquez**, who did not receive starts today. We are keeping a close watch on **Dillon Dingler**, whose 50.38 score is heavily reliant on wind factors; if the wind dies down in Chicago, he may become a liability compared to the safer profiles of **Kazuma Okamoto** or **Colt Keith**, both of whom are projected for strong performances in their respective matchups.",
